    skos:definition "dried plums, which are imported, to the extent of about 1000 tons a-year, from France, as a table fruit, for pies and puddings; also for medicinal uses, their properties being laxative when stewed. The largest and finest kind, the French plum or table prune, is the Catharine variety of the *Prunus domestica*, and is usually packed in cartoons; the common kind, the Julian variety, being packed in barrels. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 316]"@en ;
